  <string name="aqi_forecast_title">24-Hour AQI Forecast</string>
  <string name="aqi_advice_good">Air quality is considered satisfactory, and air pollution poses little or no risk.</string>
  <string name="aqi_advice_fair">Air quality is acceptable; however, for some pollutants there may be a moderate health concern for a very small number of people.</string>
  <string name="aqi_advice_moderate">Members of sensitive groups may experience health effects. The general public is not likely to be affected.</string>
  <string name="aqi_advice_poor">Everyone may begin to experience health effects; members of sensitive groups may experience more serious health effects.</string>
  <string name="aqi_advice_very_poor">Health warnings of emergency conditions. The entire population is more likely to be affected.</string>
  <string name="aqi_advice_extremely_poor">Extremely poor air quality. Stay indoors and keep windows closed.</string>
  <string name="aqi_health_good">It\'s a perfect day for outdoor activities and exercise. Open your windows to let fresh air in.</string>
  <string name="aqi_health_fair">Most people can continue their outdoor activities as usual. Extremely sensitive people should consider reducing prolonged or heavy exertion.</string>
  <string name="aqi_health_moderate">Sensitive groups (children, elderly, those with respiratory issues) should limit time spent outdoors. The general public is likely fine.</string>
  <string name="aqi_health_poor">Everyone should limit time spent outdoors. Keep windows closed and avoid heavy exercise outside.</string>
  <string name="aqi_health_very_poor">Avoid all outdoor physical activity. Stay indoors in a clean-air environment if possible.</string>
  <string name="aqi_health_extremely_poor">Critical air quality. Stay indoors, use air purifiers, and keep all windows and doors closed.</string>

